From 1453b3e8d2d5e0056b65dcaebb35c83fecbc44ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:22:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: on NVIDIA the display is told when a half 3D
 layout ends, and only of a layout that stays

Two changes to the HDMI vendor InfoFrame that nvidia-drm is given for
the half layouts (side-by-side and top-and-bottom).

When the layout ended, the InfoFrame was taken away: the display got no
vendor InfoFrame any more and had to notice by that. Some displays do
not, and go on showing a 2D picture as two eyes (HDMI 2.0, appendix F).
The kernel's own HDMI code, which i915 uses, sends an InfoFrame that
says "no 3D" (HDMI_Video_Format 0) in every 2D mode for that reason, and
amdgpu, with the patches of this tree, sends one when a 3D layout ends.
The driver is now given that one (03 0C 00 00) with the
commit that ends the layout, and keeps it in the modes that are set
later, until a layout is told again or Kodi ends. It is taken away with
a mode for which the driver sends a vendor InfoFrame of its own, which
ours would be sent in place of: a frame-packed mode, and a mode with an
HDMI_VIC (2160p at 24 to 30 Hz). If the driver does not take it, the
InfoFrame of the layout is taken away as before, from then on.

Native Dolby Vision output uses the same property, and does not start
while something else has it. The "no 3D" InfoFrame is the one
exception: CDVBridgeState::Capture() is told its blob, puts the Dolby
one in its place and leaves the property empty when native output ends.
Without a 3D display there never is such a blob, and Capture() does what
it did.

A Kodi that ends while the driver has an InfoFrame of its 3D output
leaves it on the connector (a later commit takes it away where Kodi
ends by itself). The next Kodi clears it with its first modeset, as it
clears what native Dolby Vision output left; its log line now says that
it may be either.

The InfoFrame of a layout was also given while another way of drawing
waited for the next frame. Leaving the split mode sets the resolution
twice: the display was told of a layout by the first commit and of its
end by the second. It is now given under the condition that the 3D mode
of a resolution is asked for under.

Host test: drmstereo_test (the bytes, and the modes that have an
HDMI_VIC). None of this has run on a GPU.
